{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016NQAoYRHE5U4eX69NQj12t","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"b439966ee59c5a9d0cc569942c6fb6d98bb28ba4","date":"2026-10-02T18:01:58+03:00","message":"(docs) Rewrite the openmrs CLI README around how it's used (#1905)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"240212209388de52b020bdad3d5760f23946e451","date":"2026-09-29T23:56:19+03:00","message":"(chore) Adopt the shared Prettier configuration (#1892)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a2a536e17fb35333b26552436803d3a34df75ef2","date":"2026-09-29T21:44:28+03:00","message":"(fix) Check IPv4 loopback explicitly when selecting ports (#1915)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"537fb7b349faddd5785b4800a97f7bb9fa65b6ef","date":"2026-09-29T21:39:47+03:00","message":"(fix) Stop precompressing source maps in openmrs build (#1916)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd","date":"2026-09-29T12:11:09+03:00","message":"(fix) Let openmrs develop pick a port on hosts without IPv6 (#1903)","refs":"","body":"isPortAvailable binds the port on both localhost and ::1, and treated any\nerror from the ::1 bind as the port being taken. On a host with IPv6\ndisabled, that bind fails with EAFNOSUPPORT for every port, so\n`openmrs develop --port <n>` always reported the port as in use and\n`openmrs develop` without --port scanned every port up to 65535 and gave\nup.\n\nWe now only treat the ::1 bind as a conflict when the error means\nsomething is actually listening there. EAFNOSUPPORT (IPv6 disabled) and\nEADDRNOTAVAIL (IPv6 enabled but no ::1 on the loopback) fall back to the\nIPv4 result.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0119NcFRAE7ZNsubL4edUik3\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20","date":"2026-09-28T14:08:46-04:00","message":"(BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework (#1894)","refs":"","body":"* (BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework\n\nRetains a small compatibility shim with the most commonly-used public\nfunctions now stubbed. These deprecated shims will be removed in a\nfuture version.\n\nThe biggest breaking change is the framework no longer supports rxjs\ndirectly. Functions that returned Observables now return Promises. A\nsmall compatibility patch is provided for the notifications system.\n\n* Fix `getCurrentUser`'s opts\n\n* Remove isLoginEnabled\n\n* Sounder re-implementation of getCurrentUser()\n\n* Remove more stuff, add back a couple of drop APIs we need, and re-add mocks\n\n* More clean-up\n\n* Add a changeset gentle-jars-pull.md\n\n* (chore) Add docs\n\n* Clean-up README and _main-content.scss\n\n* Fixup changesets","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"}],"totalCount":6}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2014ae2-1cc2-4fad-955e-d013bb253510","uuid":"605910f2-8b9c-48c9-bc1e-e3dc197f6b74","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:10:43.693Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"b439966ee59c5a9d0cc569942c6fb6d98bb28ba4","date":"2026-10-02T18:01:58+03:00","message":"(docs) Rewrite the openmrs CLI README around how it's used (#1905)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"240212209388de52b020bdad3d5760f23946e451","date":"2026-09-29T23:56:19+03:00","message":"(chore) Adopt the shared Prettier configuration (#1892)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a2a536e17fb35333b26552436803d3a34df75ef2","date":"2026-09-29T21:44:28+03:00","message":"(fix) Check IPv4 loopback explicitly when selecting ports (#1915)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"537fb7b349faddd5785b4800a97f7bb9fa65b6ef","date":"2026-09-29T21:39:47+03:00","message":"(fix) Stop precompressing source maps in openmrs build (#1916)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd","date":"2026-09-29T12:11:09+03:00","message":"(fix) Let openmrs develop pick a port on hosts without IPv6 (#1903)","refs":"","body":"isPortAvailable binds the port on both localhost and ::1, and treated any\nerror from the ::1 bind as the port being taken. On a host with IPv6\ndisabled, that bind fails with EAFNOSUPPORT for every port, so\n`openmrs develop --port <n>` always reported the port as in use and\n`openmrs develop` without --port scanned every port up to 65535 and gave\nup.\n\nWe now only treat the ::1 bind as a conflict when the error means\nsomething is actually listening there. EAFNOSUPPORT (IPv6 disabled) and\nEADDRNOTAVAIL (IPv6 enabled but no ::1 on the loopback) fall back to the\nIPv4 result.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0119NcFRAE7ZNsubL4edUik3\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20","date":"2026-09-28T14:08:46-04:00","message":"(BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework (#1894)","refs":"","body":"* (BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework\n\nRetains a small compatibility shim with the most commonly-used public\nfunctions now stubbed. These deprecated shims will be removed in a\nfuture version.\n\nThe biggest breaking change is the framework no longer supports rxjs\ndirectly. Functions that returned Observables now return Promises. A\nsmall compatibility patch is provided